{
  "slug": "scientific-coding-skill",
  "name": "Scientific Coding Skill",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Scientific code serves truth, not users. This plugin encodes the principles that follow from that distinction: fail loudly instead of silently, require explicit parameters instead of dangerous defaults, prioritize correctness over convenience.\n\nLLMs overfit on industry code maintaining uptime rather than being truthseeking and this can silently fail your scientific experiments. This skill helps nudge coding agents in the right direction.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **1 skill**, `scientific-coding` (Rules for writing scientific and research code).\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install scientific-coding-skill@claude-community` from `cemde/Scientific-Coding-Skill`.\n\nA Claude Code plugin that teaches Claude to write correct scientific code.",
